                <pb facs="0428" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.00/832: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-27T11:00:00-00:44">June 27, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>89. My 88, June 25, 4 p.m. Barclay sent the documents to the Legation this
                    morning and inquired as to their authenticity. I replied that they were
                    forgeries and asked what steps the Liberian Government was taking to ascertain
                    their source.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
